{"chunk_id": "7a10a9a6d94b", "text": "Arjuna, burning with grief and fury over Abhimanyu\u2019s death, vows before Krishna that he will slay Jayadratha the next day even if all gods and creatures protect him. He boasts of the irresistible power of his Gandiva bow and the divine weapons he has received from the gods, declaring that he will cut through Drona\u2019s formation and reach his target. His speech mixes wrath, confidence, and devotion to Krishna, whom he credits as the source of victory. That night neither Krishna nor Arjuna can sleep, and terrifying omens shake the world, foreshadowing immense slaughter. Krishna then goes to comfort Subhadra and Abhimanyu\u2019s widow, explaining that the fallen hero has attained the glorious destiny of a true Kshatriya.\nArjuna vows to break through Drona\u2019s forces and slay Jayadratha the next day, boasting that no power in the universe can prevent it.\nThemes: warrior vow, vengeance for Abhimanyu, confidence in divine support, battle prophecy", "vector": [-0.0025885661598294973, -0.016973339021205902, -0.015389512293040752, 0.021619228646159172, -0.0013850231189280748, 0.021078089252114296, -0.024905668571591377, -0.005035247653722763, -0.010816213674843311, -0.0067840563133358955, 0.023176658898591995, 0.013884877786040306, 0.0142940329387784, -0.007206409703940153, 0.006361702457070351, 0.02792813815176487, 0.0486498661339283, -0.006589377298951149, 0.0316765271127224, -0.024892469868063927, 0.0016159977531060576, 0.00045699990005232394, 0.015891058370471, 0.02160602994263172, 0.0022915988229215145, 0.022147171199321747, -0.012433036230504513, -0.02623872272670269, 0.016828155145049095, -0.0022816997952759266, 0.0007481929496861994, 0.0011812704615294933, -0.0004011122800875455, 0.0011499238898977637, -0.028852036222815514, 0.01016948465257883, -0.005959146656095982, -0.01490116585046053, 0.013416328467428684, 0.004840569104999304, 0.013726495206356049, -0.002567118499428034, -0.019837424159049988, 0.001399046625010